"<table><tr><td class=\"es-t\">siempre</td><td>always</td></tr><tr><td class=\"es-t\">todos los días</td><td>every day</td></tr><tr><td class=\"es-t\">muchas veces</td><td>often</td></tr><tr><td class=\"es-t\">a veces</td><td>sometimes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"es-t\">pocas veces</td><td>rarely</td></tr><tr><td class=\"es-t\">nunca</td><td>never</td></tr><tr><td class=\"es-t\">dos veces a la semana</td><td>twice a week</td></tr><tr><td class=\"es-t\">cinco veces al día</td><td>five times a day</td></tr></table>\n <div class=\"ojo\">If <b>nunca</b> comes after the verb, you also need <b>no</b>: <span class=\"es-t\">Nunca tomo pescado.</span> = <span class=\"es-t\">No tomo nunca pescado.</span></div>\n <p>Days of the week with the article: <span class=\"es-t\">el lunes</span> = on Monday (this one), <span class=\"es-t\">los lunes</span> = on Mondays (every). <span class=\"es-t\">De lunes a viernes</span> = Monday to Friday.</p>",
